B.FU=new A.ha("Who Led the Covenanters?","The Covenanters had no single leader but were driven by Presbyterian ministers and nobles who opposed the Crown's interference in Scottish worship. Key figures included Archibald Campbell, Marquess of Argyll, and Richard Cameron, whose followers became known as the Cameronians.")
B.FT=new A.ha("Who Signed the National Covenant?","The National Covenant was signed by thousands of ordinary Scots at Greyfriars Kirk in 1638, not by any royal figure. Copies were sent across Scotland for more signatures. It was a grassroots act of defiance against the Crown, not a royal decree. The original document is still on display at the Greyfriars Museum.")
