B.FX=new A.ha("Lord Advocate","The Lord Advocate was Scotland's chief legal officer, responsible for prosecuting crimes on behalf of the Crown. McKenzie used this powerful position to lead the relentless persecution of the Covenanters, overseeing trials that sent hundreds to imprisonment, transportation, or death.")
B.FW=new A.ha("The Scottish Witch Trials","McKenzie gained early notoriety for his involvement in the Scottish Witch Trials, particularly his defence of an alleged witch named Maevia. Unusually for the time, he argued against the charges, demonstrating his sharp legal mind. Scotland saw over 3,800 people accused of witchcraft between the 16th and 18th centuries.")
B.FZ=new A.ha("Aretina (1660)","McKenzie wrote 'Aretina', a romantic work often considered the first Scottish novel. It was published in 1660 and showed a very different side to the man who would later become infamous for his cruelty. He was also a prolific essayist and legal writer.")
B.FY=new A.ha("The Advocates Library","McKenzie played a key role in establishing the Advocates Library in 1689, which served as Scotland's leading legal library. It later evolved into the National Library of Scotland, one of the country's most important cultural institutions, housing millions of items.")
